  "prefLabel": "Cul-H 102.01 Agency",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Cul-H 102.01 “Agency” means “agency” as defined by RSA 541-A:1, II, namely “each state board, commission, department, institution, officer, or any other state official or group, other than the legislature or the courts, authorized by law to make rules or determine contested cases.” Here, “agency” refers to the division of historical resources.\n\nSource. #10217, eff 10-30-12, EXPIRED: 7-1-18",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/cul-h100.html"
